# PostHog product analytics.
# Both are PUBLIC client-side keys (safe to expose in the browser bundle).
# Copy this file to .env and these values are already correct for project 522643.
#
# `.env` is gitignored, so BOTH must also exist in the Vercel project
# (henneth-site -> Settings -> Environment Variables) or the production build ships
# without analytics. src/components/posthog.astro refuses to initialise when the token
# is absent, so a missing variable surfaces as "no data in PostHog" — never as a build
# error. Nothing will tell you; you have to know to look.
#
# SCOPE THEM TO PRODUCTION. Every Vercel preview deployment builds in production mode,
# so a Preview-scoped token pours preview traffic into the same project as real
# visitors — which is exactly what happened to GA4 on this site once already (see the
# note above the gtag block in src/layouts/Base.astro). posthog.astro carries a runtime
# hostname guard as the second lock, but the variable scope is the first one.
#
# Being PUBLIC keys, neither needs Vercel's "Sensitive" flag — that only prevents you
# from reading the value back later, and both ship in the HTML of every page anyway.
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=phc_wU2HSFb2bsTr7ngo3noCJsgscF8dvcXW34DXJH3rZxjb
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
